WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.567
Classes.

2
00:00:01.867 --> 00:00:07.200
A class bundles data and behavior together, so your code can model real things clearly.

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.700
A class bundles state and behavior into one blueprint.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.667
The init method runs at construction and sets up the new instance.

5
00:00:15.967 --> 00:00:17.663
And self is that instance.

6
00:00:17.663 --> 00:00:20.533
Python passes it to every method explicitly.

7
00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:23.433
Here's the life of an object.

8
00:00:23.733 --> 00:00:25.200
The class is the blueprint.

9
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.900
Each time you call it, Python runs init.

10
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.133
And out comes a new instance with its own attributes.

11
00:00:32.333 --> 00:00:36.033
Dunder methods connect your objects to Python's built-in features.

12
00:00:36.333 --> 00:00:38.600
Repr controls what debugging shows you.

13
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.367
And eq defines what double equals means for your objects.

14
00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:44.800
Here's a small class.

15
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.667
Init stores the name and diameter on self.

16
00:00:47.967 --> 00:00:51.633
Repr returns a readable string, instead of a memory address.

17
00:00:51.933 --> 00:00:54.533
Now printing an asteroid shows something useful.

18
00:00:55.733 --> 00:00:59.967
Build two asteroids with identical data, and one more idea appears.

19
00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:04.267
Once eq is defined, double equals compares the data, and says True.

20
00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:08.867
But is checks identity, and those are two separate objects, so it says False.

21
00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:12.200
Here's why this matters in a RAG system.

22
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:17.467
Every retrieved passage is a Chunk object with text, source, page, and score.

23
00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:22.500
A good repr turns debug logs into readable lines, not memory addresses.

24
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.600
And eq lets your tests assert exactly which chunks were retrieved.

25
00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:28.577
Let's recap.

26
00:01:28.577 --> 00:01:30.067
A class is a blueprint.

27
00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:32.400
Init and self set up each instance.

28
00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.167
Dunder methods hook into Python's built-ins.

29
00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:39.563
And double equals compares value while is compares identity.

30
00:01:39.563 --> 00:01:41.133
Next up: encapsulation.
